  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A rod of length <math><mn>50</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>m</mi></math> is pivoted at one end. It is raised such that it makes an angle of <math><msup><mrow><mn>30</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>o</mi></mrow></msup></math> from the horizontal as shown and released from rest. Its angular speed when it passes through the horizontal (in <math><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><msup><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> ) will be <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><msup><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><img height=\"196\" src=\"assets\\qt0200_6b21af7f3ec4.png\" width=\"286\" /></p>"
  },
